course: dictionary
lesson: 7419
title: Police and what they do
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The police are the people whose job is to keep everyone safe, help people in danger and make sure the laws are kept. A police officer is one person who works for the police. Police is a group word, so we say the police are, even when we mean many people.
explain: Read the words around police to find its meaning. «After a serious street fight the police may visit the family at home.» A serious fight is something dangerous or against the law, so the police come to help and check what happened.
explain: If you are lost or in danger, find a police officer or a trusted adult and ask for help. In an emergency, call the police: 999 in the UK and Ireland, 911 in the USA and Canada, 000 in Australia, or 111 in New Zealand.
fact: «Police» means the people whose job is to keep everyone safe and make sure the laws are kept.
fact: A «police officer» is one person who works for the police.
fact: The police are a group word, so it takes are: «the police are coming».
fact: «Real police do not ask for payment by message or phone»; a «pay or be arrested» message is a scam.
fact: In an emergency, call 999 in the UK and Ireland, 911 in the USA and Canada, 000 in Australia, or 111 in New Zealand.
exercise: «A police officer came round and gave him a warning.» What is a police officer? | A teacher at a school | *One person who works for the police | A car that goes very fast | The whole police force gathered in one place
exercise: «Real police do not ask for payment by message or phone.» Which is true? | Police ask for money in every text | Police send payment requests to your phone | *Real police do not ask for payment by message or phone | A message asking you to pay by phone is always real
exercise: «Small details like a car's colour, a number plate or what someone wore help police a lot.» Find and copy one word that means the people who keep us safe. | *police | details | number | colour
test: If you are lost, which of these is a safe person to ask for help? | A message on your phone asking for money | A stranger who offers you a ride | Someone in a hurry on a bike | *A police officer
test: Which number do you call in an emergency in the USA? | *911 | 000 | 999 | 111
exam: A message says, «Pay now or be arrested.» What should you do? | Send your bank details to the sender | Reply and ask for more time | Pay straight away to be safe | *Tell a trusted adult, because real police do not ask for payment by message or phone
